@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+---
+name: open-artlite-regressions
+description: Rebuild and validate the dense-model fixes from OpenFlowLM issue 212, including missing small-model exports, Llama batched attention, Q8 embedding rows and shared prefill weight buffers. Use for regressions or follow-up measurements on these paths.
+---
+
+Use [the validation report](../../../specs/open-engine/issue-212-validation.md) for measured limits and the fixed prompt inputs. Do not infer a full model or release-package pass from a kernel compile.
+
+The release exporter discovers every JSON file under `open_kernels/recipes/specs`.
+The added specs are `llama32-1b`, `llama32-3b` and `qwen3-0.6b`; their `extra.model` must match `model_list.json` exactly. Frozen hashes and model-name tests need entries when adding another spec.
+
+On native Windows, activate the installed IRON environment (locally `C:/dev/mlir-aie/iron_env.ps1`: mlir-aie 1.4.2, Peano 21.0.0.2026080301+c9c5ecb7). Keep Peano's bin off PATH. Build each **complete** model set, including GGUF twins and all attention tiers:
+
+```powershell
+python open_kernels/export_qwen36_kernels.py --spec open_kernels/recipes/specs/llama32-1b.json -j4
+python open_kernels/export_qwen36_kernels.py --spec open_kernels/recipes/specs/llama32-3b.json -j4
+python open_kernels/export_qwen36_kernels.py --spec open_kernels/recipes/specs/qwen3-0.6b.json -j4
+python open_kernels/export_qwen36_kernels.py --spec open_kernels/recipes/specs/llama31-8b.json -j4
+```
+
+This produced complete `manifest.json` + `toolchain.json` exports on Windows on 2026-10-22. Do not use `--only` or `OPEN_KERNELS_UNVALIDATED` to declare a packaged model complete. On Linux the full default CMake preset/export remains the release authority; that aggregate Linux package was not built in this Windows run. Built xclbins stay ignored.
+
+Standalone native host build:
+
+```powershell
+cmake -S src/open_qwen36 -B build-issue212 -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DXRT_INCLUDE_DIR=C:/dev/XRT/src/runtime_src/core/include -DXRT_LIB_DIR=C:/dev/xrtNPUfromDLL
+cmake --build build-issue212 --config Release --target open_qwen36_cli manifest_test q4nx_file_test block_host_test -j4
+ctest --test-dir build-issue212 -C Release -R "Q4NX-EMBED|OPEN-MANIFEST" --output-on-failure
+python open_kernels/model/replica_block.py --fixture build-issue212/block-fixture
+build-issue212/Release/block_host_test.exe build-issue212/block-fixture
+```
+
+The standalone CLI delay-loads VCOMP140 so Core can set passive OpenMP waiting before runtime initialization. For matched runs also set `OMP_WAIT_POLICY=PASSIVE` in the parent environment. Use `python -X utf8 utilities/generate-registry.py ...` on Windows to avoid a spurious generated-header encoding change.
+
+Llama prefill uses `prep=rope`, the manifest's scaled inverse frequencies, and two score **and probability** passes (BF16 high + remainder). A single BF16 probability pass failed the longer-prompt gate; do not remove the remainder to improve the timing. K2/Qwen keep their existing probability route.
+
+Use `OFLM_OPEN_ATTN_BLOCK=0` for the per-token attention control and `=1` for batched attention. This switches attention only; both use batched projection GEMMs. `compare-open-logits.py --exact` is appropriate for buffer sharing. Route changes also need `prefill-ref-q4nx.py`: the old NPU route itself differs from the CPU oracle at near ties. Preserve failing short-prompt results when adding a broader sample.
+
+`benchmark-open-cli.py` interleaves builds/routes on identical token IDs, rejects failed or mismatched runs, saves executable/model/manifest hashes and raw logs, excludes warmups, and reports medians/ranges. These are engine prefill/decode timings, not HTTP TTFT or a Linux Strix Halo comparison. Avoid overlapping other NPU work with measurements.
+
+Shared weight views retain their XRT parent allocation. Never alias a `from=pack` weight: it has a distinct layout and still needs storage. The allocation log separates shared bytes from new allocations; do not add `prefill_shared` to the physical total. It excludes instruction buffers, XRT internals and host scratch.
+
+Q8 embeddings are `I8 [row_tiles, col_tiles, 8704]`, with 32x256 tiles, BF16 scales and signed codes. Decode only the requested row without requantizing. Keep all engine embedding call sites on `WeightFile::embed_row`, including layer-major and L-row paths. The upstream 27B header was inspected; full upstream-model inference remains a separate integration gate.
